  "root_cause": {
    "text": "In the x86/efi subsystem, `efi_free_boot_services()` was called before deferred struct page initialization completed, causing `memblock_free_late()` to skip freeing pages in uninitialized memory regions.",
    "evidence": "The CVE description states that with CONFIG_DEFERRED_STRUCT_PAGE_INIT=y, `efi_free_boot_services()` is called before deferred initialization of the memory map is complete, and `memblock_free_late()` skips uninitialized pages, resulting in a memory leak. The patch resolves this by splitting the function to defer actual freeing until `arch_initcall` time after initialization is complete.",
    "passed_review": true
  },
